  "note": "Greater Fort Lauderdale joined as the THIRTY-SECOND market at 85 published pet-friendly profiles over 10 publishing corridors (coral-springs-coconut-creek, cypress-creek, dania-beach, deerfield-beach, fll-airport-sr84, fort-lauderdale-beach, hollywood-beach, pembroke-pines-miramar, plantation-davie, port-everglades-17th-street), built from zero SHADOW_UNTIL_REGISTERED on the Miami-live release-factory lineage, closed in that same order through the supported attended-browser lane to 0 actionable unresolved rows, registered against the Miami-live parent as COMPOSITE_FRESH_MARKET_DATA_ONLY with 15/15 registration checks and 0 broad regression runs, and founder-authorized on 2026-09-21 with all 323 unresolved identities HELD (90 routing, 89 access-blocked behind brand anti-bot walls, 69 silent on their own pages, 38 open on identity including four dual-brand halves, 37 evidence holds) and 53 verified-no-pets rows kept as exclusions rather than profiles. The exact authorized artifact was deployed with no rebuild; the live sitemap hashes to the authorized candidate and all 2711 live routes return 200, with every one of the 376 held and verified-no-pets Fort Lauderdale rows confirmed 404 and all 2614 routes the parent served individually reconfirmed. Registration had to repair a cross-market exclusion collision at its source -- a DBPR bare chain flag in Miramar was barring Cleveland's Holiday Inn Express & Suites in Westlake OH -- and that Cleveland profile is verified 200 and byte-identical after this deploy. The other 8 corridors stay below their own publication minimum and were not forced. Rollback is the deployment Fort Lauderdale replaced (Miami-live, 31 markets).",
